course: dictionary
lesson: 7838
title: Words about fairness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how people are treated. Racially is one of them. It means in a way that is connected with race: the groups people are sometimes put into because of their skin colour, family background, or where their families come from. «The class is racially mixed, with children whose families come from many different countries.» Mixed means the class has many different backgrounds, and that is worth noticing.
explain: Context can show you the feeling in a word. «Three players were racially abused online.» Abused means treated badly, and racially tells you it was because of their race. That is wrong, and it is often against the law. When you read a sentence like this, ask: who was treated badly, and why?
explain: Use the swap check to test your meaning. Put it into the sentence: «...abused because of their race.» If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Racially means in a way that is connected with race.
fact: Race is about the groups people are sometimes divided into, because of skin colour, family background or where their families came from.
fact: «Racially mixed» means a group has people from many different backgrounds.
fact: «Racially abused» means treated badly because of race, which is wrong and often against the law.
fact: Treating people unfairly because of race is called racism, and schools teach that it is wrong.
exercise: «The class is racially mixed.» What does racially mixed mean? | A class where everyone wears the same uniform | A noisy class with loud music | *A group with children from many different backgrounds | A class with only one child in it
exercise: «Three players were racially abused online.» What does racially tell you here? | *The abuse was because of their race | The players were very fast runners | The game was played in the rain | The players were all wearing the same shirt
exercise: A hateful post appears online. What is the right move? | *Report it, not share it | Add a comment with more hate | Share it with all your friends | Report it
test: «The history lesson was about places that were racially segregated.» What does segregated mean here? | Painted in bright colours | *Kept apart because of race | Very old and crumbling | Joined together for a big party
test: Treating people unfairly because of their race is called what? | Recess | *Racism | Rarity | Racing
exam: A class has children from many countries, so it is ___ mixed. | quietly | happily | *racially | suddenly
